e prepositions of place to say where places are in a city."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's meet at the store. <br/> It's on the corner."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Preposition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in Madrid\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"at\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"at the store\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on the corner\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"next to \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"next to that building\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in front of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in front of the hospital\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The preposition comes after the verb and before the noun. They answer the question <span class=\"italic\">\"Where?\"<span/>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Where is the hospital? <br/> It's in front of the train station."}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the city."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving Directions Using the Imperative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the modal <span class=\"strong\">could</span> to ask for directions.  <br/> You can use the Imperative to give directions. When you use Imperatives, you give commands."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Excuse me, where is the hospital?<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Passerby</span>: Take the first street on the left. Walk straight for two blocks. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Could you tell me where the hospital is? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Passerby</span>: It's in the vicinity of the park. You could take the bus there."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "vicinity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the area close to a place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are a lot of shops in the vicinity of the hotel."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "neighborhood"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area of a city where people live"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd like to live here. This is a beautiful neighborhood."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "traffic light"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "green, red and yellow lights used to control traffic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Go straight when the traffic light turns green."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lovely"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "beautiful; attractive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's a lovely necklace."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "parking lot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area for parking cars"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to put my car in the parking lot."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hospital"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a building where sick people are treated"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: His leg is broken. He is in the hospital."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le05ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose your favorite place in your city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a blog entry (5-8 lines) about the place and say why you like it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write instructions for how to get there."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your blog to your partner, and give them directions to the place."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I describe places in my city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements in a blog entry."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express location and give directions in writing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I tell my partner directions to my favorite place."}]}]}